[rvn-ple] Accept a grafted MTP draft head in the RVN text contract

rvn-w4a16 only. The shipped candidate /models/rvn-qwen38-ple-nvfp4 carries no
draft layer, so the text contract refuses anything MTP-shaped three times
over: assert_rvn_text_config rejects a non-zero count, Qwen4ExpForCausalLM
then asserts rvn_mtp_count(config) == 0, and its loader runs every weight
name through reject_non_text_weight_name, which raises on any name containing
"mtp". That is correct for the candidate and fatal for a grafted copy of it,
which is what this patch serves: the same base shards (hardlinked), the
source checkpoint's top-level mtp.* tensors copied byte-identically, and a
config.json that declares mtp_num_hidden_layers 1 plus the graft tool's stamp
rvn_mtp_graft = {source, encoder_version: "rvn-mtp-graft-r1", count: 1}.

One predicate, rvn_mtp_graft_active(config) = count == 1 AND the stamp's
encoder_version is the frozen literal AND its count is 1, is the only new
authority; all three parts must line up, because the weights themselves are
unverifiable copies and nothing in the tensor names distinguishes a graft
from a stray tensor. Every other shape keeps the old behaviour verbatim:
count > 1, an unstamped non-zero count, a foreign encoder_version or a
stamp whose count disagrees still raise the existing "must declare zero MTP
layers" message, and reject_non_text_weight_name's default stays strict so
claim_text_weight_name, the inventory tooling and the existing suites see no
change. Visual names are refused with or without the stamp.

The stamp relaxes the raise, never the skip: the target loader keeps
`if "mtp" in name: continue`, which is where the draft tensors are dropped,
so Qwen4ExpForCausalLM never allocates a draft head -- it just stops
treating the draft's weights as a contract violation. normalize_text_config
stops pinning mtp_num_hidden_layers to 0 for a stamped config, because that
pin would hide the layer patch 0059's draft remap keys on.

NEXTN is lossless against the target, so a grafted head that matches the
target poorly can only cost acceptance rate, never correctness; that is why
serving it is a loader question and not a training one.

--- a/python/sglang/srt/models/qwen4_exp_text_adapter.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/models/qwen4_exp_text_adapter.py
@@ -26,6 +26,12 @@ RVN_TEXT_MODEL_TYPE = "qwen4_exp_text"
 MULTIMODAL_ARCHITECTURE = "Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration"
 MTP_DRAFT_ARCHITECTURE = "Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP"
 
+# Grafted-MTP stamp (patch 0058): an RVN candidate whose draft head was grafted
+# from another checkpoint declares exactly one MTP layer and carries this stamp,
+# which the graft tool writes into config.json as
+# rvn_mtp_graft = {source, encoder_version, count}.
+RVN_MTP_GRAFT_ENCODER_VERSION = "rvn-mtp-graft-r1"
+
 # Flat qwen4_exp_text fields that must survive normalization untouched:
 # sparse-attention/indexer, layer types, hyperconnection count, n-gram
 # hashing/partitioning, rotary parameters and MTP-related flags.
@@ -114,6 +120,27 @@ def rvn_mtp_count(config: Any) -> int:
     )
 
 
+def rvn_mtp_graft_active(config: Any) -> bool:
+    """True when the config declares exactly one grafted MTP draft layer.
+
+    A grafted checkpoint is the base RVN candidate plus an ``mtp.*`` head copied
+    verbatim from another checkpoint by the graft tool, so nothing here can be
+    inferred from the weights: all three parts must line up or the contract
+    falls back to the plain text-only rule (reject every mtp-named tensor).
+    Callers gate on the RVN text architecture separately; this predicate is
+    only the count-plus-stamp half of the rule, so it stays usable from the
+    config, loader and draft-selection paths without an architecture check.
+    """
+    if rvn_mtp_count(config) != 1:
+        return False
+    stamp = _field(config, "rvn_mtp_graft", None)
+    if stamp is None:
+        return False
+    if _field(stamp, "encoder_version", None) != RVN_MTP_GRAFT_ENCODER_VERSION:
+        return False
+    return int(_field(stamp, "count", 0) or 0) == 1
+
+
 def assert_rvn_text_config(config: Any) -> None:
     """Checked-wrapper invariants for the RVN text path; raises on violation."""
     if not is_rvn_text_config(config):
@@ -127,7 +154,11 @@ def assert_rvn_text_config(config: Any) -> None:
             "RVN text config must not enable vision fields: "
             f"vision_config={_field(config, 'vision_config')!r}"
         )
-    if rvn_mtp_count(config) != 0:
+    # The one exception is a grafted draft head (rvn_mtp_graft_active): exactly
+    # one layer, declared by the graft tool's stamp. Every other non-zero count
+    # -- count > 1, an unstamped config, a stamp with a foreign
+    # encoder_version or a mismatched count -- keeps the message below.
+    if rvn_mtp_count(config) != 0 and not rvn_mtp_graft_active(config):
         raise ValueError(
             "RVN text config must declare zero MTP layers, got "
             f"mtp_num_hidden_layers={_field(config, 'mtp_num_hidden_layers', 0)!r} "
@@ -142,13 +173,16 @@ def normalize_text_config(config: Any) -> dict:
     unchanged: the multimodal path must see byte-identical baseline values. RVN
     flat qwen4_exp_text configs get their text-only invariants checked and their
     MTP count pinned to 0; every field in PRESERVED_CONFIG_FIELDS keeps its
-    incoming value.
+    incoming value. A grafted draft head is the sole exception to the pin:
+    zeroing it there would hide the very layer the stamp declares, and the NEXTN
+    draft remap in configs/model_config.py keys on it.
     """
     out = config_to_dict(config)
     if not is_rvn_text_model(out.get("architectures"), out.get("model_type")):
         return out
     assert_rvn_text_config(out)
-    out["mtp_num_hidden_layers"] = 0
+    if not rvn_mtp_graft_active(out):
+        out["mtp_num_hidden_layers"] = 0
     return out
 
 
@@ -175,11 +209,19 @@ def is_mtp_weight_name(name: str) -> bool:
     return _MTP_MARK in name
 
 
-def reject_non_text_weight_name(name: str) -> None:
-    """Text-prefix-only checkpoint rule for the RVN arch: no visual/MTP tensors."""
+def reject_non_text_weight_name(name: str, allow_mtp: bool = False) -> None:
+    """Text-prefix-only checkpoint rule for the RVN arch: no visual/MTP tensors.
+
+    ``allow_mtp`` is the grafted-draft escape hatch: it is set by the target
+    loader only when ``rvn_mtp_graft_active(config)`` holds, and it merely stops
+    the raise -- the loader still ``continue``s past every mtp-named tensor, so
+    the target never allocates a draft head. Visual names are refused either
+    way, and the default stays strict so every other caller (claim_text_weight_name,
+    the inventory tooling, the tests) keeps the original contract.
+    """
     if is_visual_weight_name(name):
         raise ValueError(f"RVN text checkpoint must not contain visual weights: {name}")
-    if is_mtp_weight_name(name):
+    if is_mtp_weight_name(name) and not allow_mtp:
         raise ValueError(f"RVN text checkpoint must not contain MTP weights: {name}")
 
 
